## Analysis

Let $\Omega$ be the root set of $f$ in $M$. Since $f$ is irreducible over $K$ and $M/K$ is Galois, $G$ acts transitively on $\Omega$. Since $L/K$ is Galois, $H = \operatorname{Gal}(M/L) \trianglelefteq G$. The irreducible factors $f_1,\dots,f_k$ over $L$ correspond to the $H$-orbits on $\Omega$. Because $H$ is normal, $G$ permutes these orbits, so all factors have the same degree. The question is whether the $H$-set structures on different orbits are isomorphic.

For $\Omega_j = g(\Omega_i)$, the action of $H$ on $\Omega_j$ is isomorphic to the action on $\Omega_i$ *twisted* by the automorphism $h \mapsto g^{-1}hg$. These need not be isomorphic to the untwisted action. A concrete counterexample shows this.

